  {
   "id": 497477,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Identify the following statement as the converse, inverse, or contrapositive: “If Dora is not an explorer, then Boots is not a monkey.”",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The original statement:</p>\n<p>If Dora is an explorer, then Boots is a monkey.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p\"></span>: Dora is an explorer.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"q\"></span>: Boots is a monkey.</p>\n<p>In symbols, the original statement is <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The new statement:</p>\n<p>If Dora is not an explorer, then Boots is not a monkey.</p>\n<p>In symbols, the new statement is <span data-math=\"{\\sim}p \\rightarrow {\\sim}q\"></span>.</p>\n<p>This is the inverse of the original statement. The inverse negates each statement but does not change the order.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Inverse"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 497478,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Identify the following statement as the converse, inverse, or contrapositive: “If Boots is a monkey, then Dora is an explorer.”",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The original statement:</p>\n<p>If Dora is an explorer, then Boots is a monkey.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p\"></span>: Dora is an explorer.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"q\"></span>: Boots is a monkey.</p>\n<p>In symbols, the original statement is <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The new statement:</p>\n<p>If Boots is a monkey, then Dora is an explorer.</p>\n<p>In symbols, the new statement is <span data-math=\"q \\rightarrow p\"></span>.</p>\n<p>This is the converse of the original statement. A converse changes the order of the original statement.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Converse"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 497479,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which statement is logically equivalent to the inverse?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The inverse and the converse are equivalent. To show that two statements are logically equivalent, construct a truth table for a biconditional using the first statement as the hypothesis (the inverse, <span data-math=\"{\\sim}p \\rightarrow {\\sim}q)\"></span> and the second statement (the converse, <span data-math=\"q \\rightarrow p\"></span>) as the conclusion. If the last column holds true only, the statements are equivalent.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\sim}p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\sim}q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\sim}p \\rightarrow {\\sim}q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q \\rightarrow p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"({\\sim}p \\rightarrow {\\sim}q) \\leftrightarrow (q \\rightarrow p)\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The inverse and converse are equivalent since the last column is always true.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Converse"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
